        "original_id": "f9f1edbe-9ec4-5dcc-b5e5-6a22473607bf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: H. G. Wells, Rubén Darío\n- Products: Love and Mr Lewisham\n- Concepts: modernismo, modernism\n\nFacts:\n- H. G. Wells was born on 21 September 1866 and was an English writer.\n- Rubén Darío was born as Félix Rubén García Sarmiento on January 18, 1867 and was a Nicaraguan poet.\n- Love and Mr Lewisham is a 1900 novel by H. G. Wells.\n- Love and Mr Lewisham is subtitled \"The Story of a Very Young Couple\" and is set in the 1880s.\n- Rubén Darío initiated the Spanish-American literary movement called modernismo, or modernism, which flourished at the end of the 19th century.\n- Rubén Darío died on February 6, 1916.\n- H. G. Wells died on 13 August 1946.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
